</section>

<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">Whirlpool / Maytag / KitchenAid</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Whirlpool family F-code system (shared platform).</h2>
    <p class="lead">Whirlpool, Maytag, and KitchenAid washers use the same F-code platform across front-load Duet and many HE top-load lines. The codes mean the same thing on all three brands; the parts share catalog families.</p>
    <table class="price-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Common cause</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>F0E1</td><td>Control board fault</td><td>Main control unit replacement</td></tr>
        <tr><td>F1E1</td><td>Main control unit communication</td><td>Harness or control board</td></tr>
        <tr><td>F2E1</td><td>Stuck button on UI</td><td>Membrane keypad</td></tr>
        <tr><td>F2E2</td><td>User Interface board failure</td><td>UI board (KitchenAid 2014-2019 model years common, $440-720 replacement)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>F5E1</td><td>Lid switch fault (top-load)</td><td>Washer reads the lid open when it's closed; lid switch or wiring</td></tr>
        <tr><td>F5E2</td><td>Door / lid lock</td><td>Lock can't engage; door interlock or lid lock assembly $260-440</td></tr>
        <tr><td>F5E3</td><td>Lid unlock fault (top-load)</td><td>Lock stuck, won't release the lid; lid lock assembly</td></tr>
        <tr><td>F6E1</td><td>Communication error (UI to MCU)</td><td>Harness or board</td></tr>
        <tr><td>F7E1</td><td>Motor / basket speed fault</td><td>Basket not turning as sensed; motor or motor control board</td></tr>
        <tr><td>F8E1 (LF)</td><td>No water / long fill</td><td>Inlet valve, hose, screen, water pressure, pressure switch</td></tr>
        <tr><td>F8E2</td><td>Dispenser / no water detected</td><td>Dispenser motor or clogged inlet on models with a dispenser</td></tr>
        <tr><td>F9E1 (Ld)</td><td>Long drain / drain fault</td><td>Pump motor, hose, filter (kickplate access)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sud / Sd</td><td>Excess suds</td><td>Too much detergent or non-HE soap; the washer pauses to clear foam</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>The top three we get called on are the lid-lock family (F5E1, F5E2, F5E3) on top-load HE machines, the F8E1 / LF slow-fill, and the F9E1 / Ld long-drain. The lid-lock codes are a real safety interlock: the washer will not spin until the lid genuinely locks, so a worn lock assembly stops the machine cold. Drain and fill codes usually start upstream (a kinked hose, a clogged filter, low water pressure) before they're ever the pump or valve, which is why our techs check the cheap causes first.</p>
    <p>Deep dives: <a href="/services/washer-repair/whirlpool-error-codes/">Whirlpool washer error codes</a> (Cabrio vs Duet, generation transitions) · <a href="/services/washer-repair/maytag-error-codes/">Maytag washer error codes</a> (10-yr warranty reality). Brand pillars: <a href="/brands/whirlpool-washer-repair/">Whirlpool</a> · <a href="/brands/maytag-washer-repair/">Maytag</a> · KitchenAid.</p>
  </div>
</section>

