<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">GE</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">GE mostly shows plain-language messages, not cryptic codes.</h2>
    <p>Unlike Samsung or LG, most GE washers print the problem in words — "Confirm Water Supply," "Check and Clean Drain Pump Filter," an unbalanced-load light — rather than a code. So there isn't a big GE code table to memorize; the machine already names the category. (Two exceptions: the newer GE UltraFast combo uses model-specific numeric codes, and older GE Profile front-loaders used an E-series that needs a technician.)</p>
    <table class="price-table">
      <thead><tr><th>GE says</th><th>Category</th><th>Common cause</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Check / Clean Drain Pump Filter</td><td>Drain</td><td>Filter clog, hose, drain pump motor</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Confirm Water Supply</td><td>Fill</td><td>Valves, hose, inlet screen, inlet valve</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Unbalanced / spin light</td><td>Unbalance</td><td>Load distribution; suspension if persistent</td></tr>
